  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The atom with 55 protons is caesium(Cs). The electronic configuration of Cs is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>The mono positive ion means one electron is removed from outermost orbital. Hence, the sum of electrons in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;orbitals&nbsp;are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>.</p>"
